-- תקנון שירות עובדי הוראה, פרק 1א', §1.22 שעות העבודה ומשך השיעורים
-- How long a lesson is, how long a class must stay in school, the two
-- timetables the pedagogical secretariat recommends, and who may change them.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT common

§ `1.22 שעות העבודה ומשך השיעורים`

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_22__ssec_1_22 Section heading only; its paragraphs below carry the rules.

§§ `1.22.1 משך השיעורים`

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_22__ssec_1_22__para_1 Lead-in ("the length of lessons in all institutions shall be as follows"); the rules are its sub-paragraphs.

@desc One school day of a class, as far as section 1.22 asks about it. Times are minutes after midnight (8:00 is 480).
DECLARE `school day of a class` HAS
    `lesson lengths`                   IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc the length in minutes of each of the day's first four lessons, in order
    `lessons the class studies`        IS A NUMBER  @desc how many lessons the class studies that day
    `the school is a special school`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the school gives joined lessons`  IS A BOOLEAN @desc the school gives lessons joined into a double period (שיעורים מצורפים)
    `minutes the class is in school`   IS A NUMBER  @desc from the start of the first lesson to the end of the last
    `the school has a restaurant`      IS A BOOLEAN @desc the school has a dining hall (מסעדה)

-- §1.22.1א: of the first four lessons, two are of 50 minutes and two of 45.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_22__ssec_1_22__para_1__subpara_a
GIVEN lengths IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first four lessons are two of 50 and two of 45 minutes` lengths IF
        count lengths EQUALS 4
    AND count (filter (GIVEN m YIELD m EQUALS 50) lengths) EQUALS 2
    AND count (filter (GIVEN m YIELD m EQUALS 45) lengths) EQUALS 2

-- §1.22.1ב, first sentence: the minimum time a class must be in school.
-- The 240/230 minutes are for a class "studying 4 lessons"; the 170 for a
-- special-school class "studying only 3". A class studying another number of
-- lessons has no minimum here.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_22__ssec_1_22__para_1__subpara_b
GIVEN d IS A `school day of a class`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `minimum minutes in school` d IS
    BRANCH IF d's `the school is a special school` AND d's `lessons the class studies` EQUALS 3 THEN 170
           IF d's `lessons the class studies` EQUALS 4 AND d's `the school gives joined lessons` THEN 230
           IF d's `lessons the class studies` EQUALS 4 THEN 240
           OTHERWISE 0

GIVEN d IS A `school day of a class`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the class is in school long enough` d IF
    d's `minutes the class is in school` AT LEAST `minimum minutes in school` d

DECLARE `timetable action` IS ONE OF
    `organise the lessons and breaks` HAS `the day as organised` IS A `school day of a class`
    `organise a teachers' duty roster at the end of the fourth lesson`
    `decide, with the pedagogical council, which of the first four lessons are of 50 minutes`
    `change the length of a lesson or the time of the breaks`
    `approve a change in lesson length or break times`

-- "יש לארגן" names no one; the principal is read as the one who organises
-- the school's lessons and breaks, as the same paragraph's last sentence
-- gives the principal the choice of the 50-minute lessons. The duty is ב's
-- alone: the minimum time in school (§1.22.1א's lesson lengths are their
-- own rule above, and a special-school class of 3 lessons has no fourth).
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_22__ssec_1_22__para_1__subpara_b
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `timetable action`
DECIDE `organising the day` IS
    PARTY `the school principal`
    MUST  `organise the lessons and breaks` day
          PROVIDED `the class is in school long enough` day
    LEST  BREACH BY `the school principal` BECAUSE "section 1.22.1(b): lessons and breaks must keep the class in school for the minimum time"

-- The duty roster is owed only in schools that have a restaurant.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_22__ssec_1_22__para_1__subpara_b
GIVEN d IS A `school day of a class`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `timetable action`
DECIDE `the restaurant duty roster` d IS
    IF d's `the school has a restaurant`
    THEN PARTY `the school principal`
         MUST  `organise a teachers' duty roster at the end of the fourth lesson`
         LEST  BREACH BY `the school principal` BECAUSE "section 1.22.1(b): a school with a restaurant organises a teachers' duty roster at the end of the fourth lesson"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- "The principal and the pedagogical council are empowered to decide" —
-- the council has no Party of its own here, so it is named in the action:
-- the principal decides together with it.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_22__ssec_1_22__para_1__subpara_b
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `timetable action`
DECIDE `choosing the 50-minute lessons` IS
    PARTY `the school principal`
    MAY   `decide, with the pedagogical council, which of the first four lessons are of 50 minutes`

§§ `1.22.1ג The two recommended timetables`

DECLARE `timetable slot` HAS
    `slot name`     IS A STRING
    `slot starts`   IS A NUMBER @desc minutes after midnight
    `slot ends`     IS A NUMBER @desc minutes after midnight
    `slot is a lesson` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN h IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `clock` h m IS h TIMES 60 PLUS m

GIVEN s IS A `timetable slot`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `slot length` s IS s's `slot ends` MINUS s's `slot starts`

-- The first option: two joined lessons first. "שני השיעורים הראשונים" is one
-- 90-minute slot holding two lessons of 45 minutes each.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_22__ssec_1_22__para_1__subpara_c akn:chp_1א___sec_1_22__ssec_1_22__para_1__subpara_c/p2 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_22__ssec_1_22__para_1__subpara_c/p3 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_22__ssec_1_22__para_1__subpara_c/p4 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_22__ssec_1_22__para_1__subpara_c/p5 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_22__ssec_1_22__para_1__subpara_c/p6 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_22__ssec_1_22__para_1__subpara_c/p7
`the first recommended timetable` MEANS
    LIST `timetable slot` "the first two lessons, joined" (`clock` 8 0)   (`clock` 9 30)  TRUE,
         `timetable slot` "meal break"                    (`clock` 9 30)  (`clock` 9 55)  FALSE,
         `timetable slot` "third lesson"                  (`clock` 9 55)  (`clock` 10 45) TRUE,
         `timetable slot` "break"                         (`clock` 10 45) (`clock` 11 0)  FALSE,
         `timetable slot` "fourth lesson"                 (`clock` 11 0)  (`clock` 11 50) TRUE

`the first timetable's lesson lengths` MEANS LIST 45, 45, 50, 50

@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_22__ssec_1_22__para_1__subpara_c/p8 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_22__ssec_1_22__para_1__subpara_c/p9 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_22__ssec_1_22__para_1__subpara_c/p10 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_22__ssec_1_22__para_1__subpara_c/p11 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_22__ssec_1_22__para_1__subpara_c/p12
`the second recommended timetable` MEANS
    LIST `timetable slot` "first lesson"  (`clock` 8 0)   (`clock` 8 50)  TRUE,
         `timetable slot` "second lesson" (`clock` 9 0)   (`clock` 9 50)  TRUE,
         `timetable slot` "third lesson"  (`clock` 10 15) (`clock` 11 0)  TRUE,
         `timetable slot` "fourth lesson" (`clock` 11 15) (`clock` 12 0)  TRUE

GIVEN slots IS A LIST OF `timetable slot`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `minutes from first to last` slots IS
    CONSIDER slots
    WHEN EMPTY THEN 0
    WHEN first FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        maximum (map (GIVEN s YIELD s's `slot ends`) slots) MINUS first's `slot starts`

GIVEN slots IS A LIST OF `timetable slot`
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
DECIDE `lesson slot lengths` slots IS
    map `slot length` (filter (GIVEN s YIELD s's `slot is a lesson`) slots)

-- Both recommended timetables keep the section's own rules: the first (joined
-- lessons) keeps the class in school 230 minutes, the second (all separate)
-- 240, and each has two 50-minute and two 45-minute lessons.
#ASSERT `minutes from first to last` `the first recommended timetable` EQUALS 230
#ASSERT `minutes from first to last` `the second recommended timetable` EQUALS 240
#ASSERT `lesson slot lengths` `the first recommended timetable` EQUALS LIST 90, 50, 50
#ASSERT sum `the first timetable's lesson lengths` EQUALS 190
#ASSERT `the first four lessons are two of 50 and two of 45 minutes` `the first timetable's lesson lengths`
#ASSERT `the first four lessons are two of 50 and two of 45 minutes` (`lesson slot lengths` `the second recommended timetable`)

`a day on the first timetable` MEANS
    `school day of a class` WITH
        `lesson lengths`                  IS `the first timetable's lesson lengths`
        `lessons the class studies`       IS 4
        `the school is a special school`  IS FALSE
        `the school gives joined lessons` IS TRUE
        `minutes the class is in school`  IS `minutes from first to last` `the first recommended timetable`
        `the school has a restaurant`     IS TRUE

`a day on the second timetable` MEANS
    `school day of a class` WITH
        `lesson lengths`                  IS `lesson slot lengths` `the second recommended timetable`
        `lessons the class studies`       IS 4
        `the school is a special school`  IS FALSE
        `the school gives joined lessons` IS FALSE
        `minutes the class is in school`  IS `minutes from first to last` `the second recommended timetable`
        `the school has a restaurant`     IS FALSE

#ASSERT `the class is in school long enough` `a day on the first timetable`
#ASSERT `the class is in school long enough` `a day on the second timetable`

-- The second timetable, run in a school that gives joined lessons, would need
-- only 230 minutes; a school without them that keeps classes 230 minutes falls short.
`a 230-minute day without joined lessons` MEANS
    `school day of a class` WITH
        `lesson lengths`                  IS LIST 50, 50, 45, 45
        `lessons the class studies`       IS 4
        `the school is a special school`  IS FALSE
        `the school gives joined lessons` IS FALSE
        `minutes the class is in school`  IS 230
        `the school has a restaurant`     IS FALSE

#ASSERT NOT `the class is in school long enough` `a 230-minute day without joined lessons`

#TRACE `organising the day` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the school principal` DOES `organise the lessons and breaks` `a day on the first timetable` AT 1

§§ `1.22.2`

-- F-1.22-a: §1.22.1ב empowers the principal and the pedagogical council to
-- decide which lessons are of 50 minutes; §1.22.2 makes "every change in the
-- length of a lesson" subject to the district manager's approval. Choosing a
-- lesson to be 50 rather than 45 minutes changes its length. The reading
-- adopted: §1.22.2 governs departures from §1.22.1's scheme, and the choice
-- §1.22.1ב leaves to the school is not one.
-- §1.22.2 does not forbid a change; it makes it subject to the district
-- manager's approval: without it the change may not be made, with it it may.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_22__ssec_1_22__para_2
GIVEN `the change departs from section 1.22.1's scheme` IS A BOOLEAN, `the district manager approved the change` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `timetable action`
DECIDE `changing lesson length or break times` `the change departs from section 1.22.1's scheme` `the district manager approved the change` IS
    IF `the change departs from section 1.22.1's scheme` AND NOT `the district manager approved the change`
    THEN PARTY `the school principal`
         SHANT `change the length of a lesson or the time of the breaks`
         LEST  BREACH BY `the school principal` BECAUSE "section 1.22.2: a change in lesson length or break times needs the district manager's approval"
    ELSE IF `the change departs from section 1.22.1's scheme`
         THEN PARTY `the school principal`
              MAY   `change the length of a lesson or the time of the breaks`
         ELSE `choosing the 50-minute lessons`

GIVEN `the district manager approved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a change in lesson length or break times is valid` `the district manager approved` IF
    `the district manager approved`

-- F-1.22-a's evidence: choosing which lessons are of 50 minutes is, in the
-- words of §1.22.2, a change in a lesson's length — the second timetable
-- gives the first lesson 50 minutes where the first timetable gives it 45.
`choosing the 50-minute lessons changes a lesson's length` MEANS
    NOT (at (`the first timetable's lesson lengths`) 0
         EQUALS at (`lesson slot lengths` `the second recommended timetable`) 0)
#ASSERT `choosing the 50-minute lessons changes a lesson's length`

-- An unapproved change is not valid; the school's own choice under section 1.22.1(b) is a permission.
#ASSERT NOT `a change in lesson length or break times is valid` FALSE
#TRACE `changing lesson length or break times` TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the school principal` DOES `change the length of a lesson or the time of the breaks` AT 1

§§ `1.22.3`

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_22__ssec_1_22__para_3 Pointer: further rules for kindergarten teachers are in chapter 2.1.1 of the takanon, encoded there.

